# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored (.gitignore line 2) and must stay that way. Never commit it, never paste its
# contents into an issue, a pull request or a chat message.
#
# Every setting here is optional. Without any .env at all the stack still comes up and
# diagnosis-service still answers every request - it falls back to its deterministic ranking and
# says so in the logs and in the X-Diagnosis-Mode response header.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY - the primary model diagnosis-service writes explanations with
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. It is the default provider because its quota is
# generous where OpenRouter's free tier allows 50 requests a day, which twice ran out mid-evaluation
# and left every answer coming from the deterministic scorer without that being obvious.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY - the fallback, and a second vendor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Worth setting even with a Gemini key. Gemini returns transient HTTP 503 "experiencing high demand"
# under load - every pinned flash version did so while this was being set up - and a chain that
# cannot cross vendors is barely a fallback. The two are unlikely to fail at the same moment.
# Get your own free key, which takes about two minutes:
#
#   1. Sign in at https://openrouter.ai (a GitHub account works)
#   2. Create a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
#   3. Enable prompt logging under Settings -> Privacy. The free models require it, and without it
#      every request fails with "No endpoints found matching your data policy", which looks exactly
#      like a broken key. The data sent is synthetic Sock Shop incidents, so nothing is sensitive.
#
# Use your own key rather than sharing one. The free tier allows 20 requests a minute and 50 a day
# per account (1,000 a day once an account has bought at least $10 of credits), so a shared key
# means a shared daily budget - and one person running an evaluation would exhaust it for everyone.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides - the defaults in services/diagnosis-service/app/settings.py are fine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini                                  # gemini | openrouter | ollama
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest                        # the primary model
# Tried in order when the primary is unreachable. "provider:model" crosses vendors; a bare name
# stays on the primary's provider.
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODELS=openrouter:nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free
